\begin{equation*}
D_{2E}\simeq2D_{1}\approx7\!-\!8\times10^{-6}\ {\rm Gy}\approx7.6\!-\!8.0\;
\mu{\rm Gy}\ {\rm per\ point},
\end{equation*}

$\dot D_{t}\times0.04\,{\rm s}$ total dwell, and $D_{3E}\simeq3D_{1}\approx
1.1\!-\!1.2\times10^{-5}\,{\rm Gy}\approx11\!-\!12\,\mu{\rm Gy}$ per point for
a three-energy set.  This is the local peak surface air/tissue kerma
normally quoted for the system.

In field integrated form the $W_{i}=50\,{\rm mm}$ monochromator illumination
is mapped into the $w_{f}=0.30\,{\rm mm}$ focus,

\begin{equation*}
N_{h}=W_{i}/w_{f}\simeq50/0.30\approx1.67\times10^{2},
\qquad N_{h}t_{d}\simeq3.3\ {\rm s}\ {\rm per\ energy},
\end{equation*}

independent horizontal positions.  Summed over the whole $50\times6\,{\rm mm^{2}}$
scanned Laue fan per monochromatic channel

\begin{equation*}
D_{int}\simeq N_{h}D_{1}\approx1.67\times10^{2}\times3.9\times10^{-6}\ {\rm Gy}
      \simeq6\!-\!7\times10^{-4}\ {\rm Gy}\approx0.6\!-\!0.7\ {\rm mGy},
\end{equation*}

$\approx0.64\,{\rm mGy}$ surface air/tissue kerma to the complete $50\,{\rm mm}$
Laue fan per energy, i.e. a field mean
$\langle D\rangle_{1}=D_{1}w_{f}/W_{i}\approx2\!-\!3\times10^{-8}\,{\rm Gy}
\approx20\!-\!30\,{\rm nGy}$ per energy.  With $N_{E}$ energies the
field-integrated cumulative kerma is $N_{E}D_{int}$, $\approx1.2\!-\!1.3\,{\rm mGy}$
over the $50\times6\,{\rm mm^{2}}$ line for the usual $N_{E}=2$ dual-energy
acquisition.  The $3\!-\!4\,\mu{\rm Gy}$ per $20\,{\rm ms}$ dwell is the
conventional local peak per energy per point; $N_{E}D_{1}\sim7\!-\!8\,\mu{\rm Gy}$
per point for dual energy is the customary cumulative multiple-energy
surface dose quoted for the system.  This is $0.19\,{\rm mGy\,s^{-1}}\times
0.020\,{\rm s}$ per energy per point, essentially independent of
$(\mu_{en}/\rho)$ under the $(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{t}\simeq(\mu_{en}/\rho)_{a}$
approximation. ∎
